face":"கோடு","parts":[{"text":"கோடு","lemma":"kōṭu","gloss":"blade"}],"gloss":"blade"},{"surface":"நுதி","parts":[{"text":"நுதி","lemma":"nuti","gloss":"tip"}],"gloss":"tip"},{"surface":"சிதைந்து","parts":[{"text":"சிதை","lemma":"citai","gloss":"shatter"},{"text":"ந்து","lemma":"ntu","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"having broken"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கொல்துறை","parts":[{"text":"கொல்","lemma":"kol","gloss":"killing/blacksmithing"},{"text":"துறை","lemma":"tuṟai","gloss":"place"}],"gloss":"blacksmith's workshop"},{"surface":"குற்றில","parts":[{"text":"குற்று","lemma":"kuṟṟu","gloss":"having been forged"},{"text":"இல","lemma":"இல்","gloss":"they are not"}],"gloss":"are not without being forged"},{"surface":"மாதோ","parts":[{"text":"மாதோ","lemma":"mātō","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"indeed"},{"surface":"என்றும்","parts":[{"text":"என்று","lemma":"eṉṟu","gloss":"always"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"always"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"உண்டாயின்","parts":[{"text":"உண்டு","lemma":"uṇṭu","gloss":"there is"},{"text":"ஆயின்","lemma":"āyiṉ","gloss":"if"}],"gloss":"if there is"},{"surface":"பதம்","parts":[{"text":"பதம்","lemma":"patam","gloss":"food"}],"gloss":"food"},{"surface":"கொடுத்து","parts":[{"text":"கொடு","lemma":"koṭu","gloss":"give"},{"text":"த்து","lemma":"ttu","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"having given"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இல்லாயின்","parts":[{"text":"இல்","lemma":"il","gloss":"not"},{"text":"ஆயின்","lemma":"āyiṉ","gloss":"if"}],"gloss":"if there is not"},{"surface":"உடன்","parts":[{"text":"உடன்","lemma":"uṭaṉ","gloss":"together"}],"gloss":"together"},{"surface":"உண்ணும்","parts":[{"text":"உண்","lemma":"uṇ","gloss":"eat"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"who eats"}],"gloss":"who eats"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இல்லோர்","parts":[{"text":"இல்","lemma":"il","gloss":"not having"},{"text":"ஓர்","lemma":"ōr","gloss":"people"}],"gloss":"the poor"},{"surface":"ஒக்கல்","parts":[{"text":"ஒக்கல்","lemma":"okkal","gloss":"kinfolk"}],"gloss":"kinfolk"},{"surface":"தலைவன்","parts":[{"text":"தலைவன்","lemma":"talaivaṉ","gloss":"leader"}],"gloss":"leader"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அண்ணல்எம்","parts":[{"text":"அண்ணல்எம்","lemma":"அண்ணல்எம்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கோமான்","parts":[{"text":"கோமான்","lemma":"கோமான்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வைந்","parts":[{"text":"வைந்","lemma":"வைந்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நுதி","parts":[{"text":"நுதி","lemma":"நுதி","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வேலே","parts":[{"text":"வேலே","lemma":"வேலே","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true}],"literal":"These indeed, peacock feathers adorned, garlands put on, / thick-jointed strong shafts straightened, ghee applied, / are in the well-guarded wide palace. Those indeed, / having stabbed enemies, blade-tips broken, / are in the blacksmith's workshop, not without being forged, always. / If there is food, giving it, / if there is not, eating together, / of the poor kinfolk's leader, / our noble king's sharp-tipped spears indeed!","translation":"These weapons here are adorned with peacock feathers, hung with garlands, their thick-jointed strong shafts polished, and smeared with ghee, resting in the well-guarded, spacious palace. But those weapons there, having stabbed enemies, their blade-tips shattered, are always in the blacksmith's workshop, never free from being forged. They belong to our noble king, the leader of his poor kinfolk, who shares food when there is any, and eats together with them when there is none—his sharp-tipped spears indeed!","modern":"இவை மயில் தோகைகளால் அலங்கரிக்கப்பட்டு, மாலைகள் சூட்டப்பட்டு, திரண்ட வலிமையான காம்புகள் சரிசெய்யப்பட்டு, நெய் பூசப்பட்டு, காவலுடைய அகன்ற அரண்மனையில் இருக்கின்றன. ஆனால், பகைவர்களைக் குத்தி, முனைகள் உடைந்து, எப்போதும் கொல்லனின் பட்டறையிலேயே பழுதுபார்க்கப்பட்டுக் கொண்டிருப்பவை, உணவு இருந்தால் பிறருக்குக் கொடுத்து, இல்லாதபோது அவர்களுடன் சேர்ந்து உண்ணும் வறிய சுற்றத்தாரின் தலைவனான எமது பெருமைக்குரிய அரசனின் கூர்மையான முனையையுடைய வேல்களாகும்.","explanation":"The poet Avvaiyar is speaking to King Thondaiman, who had shown her his well-stocked, pristine armory in an attempt to intimidate her and her patron, King Adhiyaman Neduman Anji. Avvaiyar compares Thondaiman's clean, unused weapons with Adhiyaman's battle-scarred ones. She points out that Thondaiman's weapons are merely decorative, kept safe in a guarded palace, whereas Adhiyaman's spears are constantly in the blacksmith's workshop being repaired because they are actively used in battle to protect his people. She praises Adhiyaman as a generous leader of the poor who shares whatever food he has with his kin. Through this contrast, she subtly warns Thondaiman of Adhiyaman's superior military experience and valor.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.3],[0.3,0.5],[0.5,0.9],[0.9,1.2],[1.2,1.9],[1.9,2.51],[2.51,3.0],[3.0,3.4],[3.4,3.8],[3.8,4.2],[4.2,5.5],[5.5,6.15],[6.15,6.3],[6.3,6.7],[6.7,7.5],[7.5,7.88],[7.88,8.2],[8.2,8.78],[8.78,9.5],[9.5,9.8],[9.8,10.4],[10.4,10.8],[10.8,11.13],[11.13,11.46],[11.46,11.8],[11.8,12.2],[12.2,12.7],[12.7,13.7],[13.7,13.9],[13.9,14.3],[14.3,14.9],[14.9,15.5],[15.5,15.8],[16.84,17.44],[17.44,17.74],[17.74,17.94],[17.94,18.34],[18.34,18.54]],"female":[[0.0,0.36],[0.36,0.6],[0.6,1.0],[1.0,1.4],[1.4,2.2],[2.2,2.81],[2.81,3.3],[3.3,3.8],[3.8,4.4],[4.4,4.7],[4.7,6.1],[6.1,6.65],[6.65,6.9],[6.9,7.3],[7.3,8.3],[8.3,8.77],[8.77,9.2],[9.2,9.4],[9.4,10.37],[10.37,11.14],[11.14,11.53],[11.53,12.3],[12.3,12.6],[12.6,12.9],[12.9,13.2],[13.2,13.6],[13.6,14.1],[14.1,14.65],[14.65,15.2],[15.2,15.5],[15.5,16.1],[16.1,16.7],[16.7,17.1],[18.32,19.02],[19.02,19.42],[19.42,19.62],[19.62,19.82],[19.82,20.12]]},"sync":[[["இவ்வே","these indeed"]],[["பீலி","peacock feathers"]],[["அணிந்து","having adorned"]],[["மாலை","garlands"]],[["சூட்டி","having put on"]],[["கண்திரள்","thick-jointed"]],[["நோன்காழ்","strong shafts"]],[["திருத்தி"